Let $x$ be the price of each shirt.  Then the total cost of the shirts is $14x$.  The total cost of the shirts, including sales tax, is $1.05(14x)$.  The total cost of the shirts, including sales tax, must be less than or equal to $\$130$, so we have the inequality $1.05(14x) \leq 130$.  Dividing both sides by $1.05$, we get $14x \leq 123.81$.  Dividing both sides by $14$, we get $x \leq 8.7$ dollars.  Since $x$ must be a whole number, the greatest possible price of a shirt is $8$ dollars.  \boxed{\text{(D)}}$

